  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On San Cha Mountain, three light pillars of yellow, blue, and red rise from the peaks when the inheritance opens, and a voice declares that Three Kings Inheritance opens that day for righteous and demonic alike. Fang Yuan treats it as three collective inheritances in one place rather than a single ordinary inheritance, names it a demonic inheritance with dog groups and checkpoints inside, and prepares bulk purchases of dog enslavement Gu, paper crane Gu, and exploding egg Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        323
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_dog_enslavement_gu",
        "gu_paper_crane_gu",
        "gu_exploding_egg_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Entry requires refining or holding the matching key Gu: dog enslavement Gu for King Quan Inheritance through the yellow pillar, paper crane Gu for King Xin Inheritance through the blue pillar, and exploding egg Gu for King Bao Inheritance through the red pillar. The three kings were rank five Gu Masters from Wang clan who rose after finding a rank six Gu Immortal inheritance and wiped Wu clan in three days.",
      "chapters": [
        324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "entry-keys",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_king_quan_inheritance",
        "inh_king_xin_inheritance",
        "inh_king_bao_inheritance",
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "fac_wang_clan",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_wu_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "News that the site had been a rank six Gu Immortal blessed land spreads and draws clans toward San Cha Mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        326
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "entry-keys",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "From the mountain foot the terrain rises into three hills like a fork, and the entrances sit above those peaks.",
      "chapters": [
        339
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "entry-keys",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan first describes the opened ground as an ancient Gu Master’s blessed land already near collapse, stripped by the three kings and then pressed further by their remodelled inheritances.",
      "chapters": [
        325
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-origin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He later tells land spirit Ba Gui that the blessed land came from an ancient strength path Gu Immortal whose dying wish formed the land spirit, and that completing the wish means refining second aperture Gu. Three roaming kids used the blessed land’s resources, became the three kings of the demonic path, failed to break through to rank six, and remodelled the place into the three kings inheritance ground before dying; they walked refinement, fire, and enslavement path, not strength path.",
      "chapters": [
        377
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-origin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ba_gui",
        "gu_second_aperture_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan tells Ba Gui he has already acquired two of the three kings inheritance once Feng Tian Yu is guided through King Xin Inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        387
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shares-and-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_feng_tian_yu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Feng Tian Yu reports clearing the hundredth round, receiving King Xin Inheritance, and taking in several hundred hairy men; talk on the peak says King Xin and King Quan Inheritance have been taken.",
      "chapters": [
        389
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shares-and-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_king_xin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo Wu Tian names King Bao as Wang Ba Dan, King Xin as Wang Xiao Ya, and King Quan as Wang Er Gou, and lists eggmen, divulge information Gu, undefeated hundred battles Gu, and the dog emperors Ying Ming and Ba Huang as the essence of the three kings inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        391
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shares-and-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
